# Matching a rule as data
#
# An N3 rule pattern asks whether an implication is present. Matching that
# quoted rule structure derives a result, showing that rules can themselves
# be inspected by rules. The only implication in this program is the rule
# itself, so the rule finds itself.

@prefix : <https://eyereasoner.github.io/ns#> .

# If any rule is present, with any premise ?A and conclusion ?B, say so.
{
    ?A => ?B .
} => {
    :result :is true .
} .
